    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0534" n="1288" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/5654</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-11T00:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 11, 1917, 12 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 9, 3 p.m. The following will be the reply of the Argentine
                    Government if formal inquiry is made.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>No restrictions will be placed on armed North American merchant vessels in
                        entering Argentine ports provided said vessels are armed solely for purpose
                        of defense of themselves. Excepting in the case of the port of Buenos Aires
                        said ships cannot bring their powder into the Argentine Republic but must
                        first place it on board an Argentine station ship near Buenos Aires while
                        the merchant vessel is in the docks.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
